Source: rate-adjusting-pcm-ring
Section: libs
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Chris Peterson <cpeter1207@users.noreply.github.com>
Build-Depends: cargo, debhelper-compat (= 13), librptadv-samplerate-adapter-dev (>= 0.1.0~alpha1), pkg-config, rustc
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Homepage: https://github.com/cpeter1207/rate_adjusting_pcm_ring
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: librate-adjusting-pcm-ring1
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}, librate-adjusting-pcm-ring2 (= ${binary:Version})
Description: ABI-compatible S16 facade for the Rust PCM ring
 Frozen ABI-major-1 shared library for existing USBRadioPlus and rpt_advanced
 consumers. Its C facade forwards to the Rust-owned rate recovery and bounded
 packet-loss-concealment implementation in ABI major two.

Package: librate-adjusting-pcm-ring-dev
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, librate-adjusting-pcm-ring1 (= ${binary:Version}), librate-adjusting-pcm-ring2-dev (= ${binary:Version})
Description: development files for the ABI-compatible S16 PCM facade
 ABI-major-1 public header and pkg-config metadata for existing dynamic
 consumers. No static archive is shipped.

Package: librate-adjusting-pcm-ring2
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}, librptadv-samplerate-adapter1 (>= 0.1.0~alpha1)
Description: lock-free canonical-F32 rate-adjusting PCM ring
 Rust shared library for single-producer/single-consumer PCM playout with
 persistent sample-rate conversion, clock recovery, and bounded concealment.

Package: librate-adjusting-pcm-ring2-dev
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, librate-adjusting-pcm-ring2 (= ${binary:Version})
Description: development files for the F32 rate-adjusting PCM ring
 Public descriptor header and pkg-config metadata for consumers of the
 dynamically linked ABI-major-2 canonical-F32 PCM ring.
